Here's the formal test smell audit of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` using the **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog**, with integration-test calibration applied (the class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`).

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` line 87  
**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // 3-second hard wait
```

**Why it's a smell even for integration tests:** A hard sleep makes the suite slow and non-deterministic — if the system responds faster or slower than 3 s, you get wasted time or a false failure.

**Fix:**
```csharp
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures; 3 s of dead wall-clock time per run compounds across suites.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` lines 101–108  
**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** One branch is **never exercised** (a newly created user won't be `PremiumUser`), so the `DiscountRate > 0` assertion is dead code providing false confidence.

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — one path is never proven.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` lines 113–119  
**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // No assertion — passes even if every row is silently lost
}
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}

var users = _repository.ListAll();
Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100 % pass rate even if the database silently drops inserts.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` lines 35–38  
**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

4 assertions with **no failure messages**. When one fails in CI, the log says only `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` — no context about _which property_ or _why_.

**Fix — add messages:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned on insert");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage in CI — developers must read source to locate the failing property.

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are **well-designed**:

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, one meaningful assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is contextually obvious (3 inserts → 3 count), `CollectionAssert` used properly |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Async integration test with proper `await` and assertion |

The setup/cleanup pattern (in-memory SQLite per test) is hermetic and correctly avoids the **Mystery Guest** smell — no external file-system or network dependency.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, …)` | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 focused tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling loop | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to assertions | ~2 min |

Fixes 1–2 directly eliminate **false-pass risk** (tests that pass when they shouldn't). Fix 3 removes flakiness and speeds up the suite. Fix 4 is a maintainability improvement for CI triage.
